---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import SideImage from '../components/SideImage.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import WorldImage from '../assets/screenshots/2023-07-28_11.57.32.png';
import EoFImage from '../assets/screenshots/2024-11-28_20.31.35.resized.png';
import NPCImage from '../assets/screenshots/npc.resized.png';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import Center from '../components/Center.astro';
import Tagline from '../components/Tagline.astro';
import Group from '../components/Group.astro';
import Stack from '../components/Stack.astro';
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import PyrrhiaMap from '../assets/Pyrrhia-Medium.png';
import PantalaMap from '../assets/Pantala-Medium.png';
import YouTubeVideo from '../components/YouTubeVideo.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import LegalDisclaimer from '../components/LegalDisclaimer.astro';
import SplitList from '../components/SplitList.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Hero />
		<Header />
		<main>
			<Stack>
				<h1>Welcome to the World of Wings of Fire!</h1>
				<p>
					Wings of Fire: The New World is a Minecraft: Java Edition dedicated server that aims to create the world of <i>Wings of Fire</i> in a large-scale, player-interactive experience.
				</p>
				<p>
					The server began in March 2016 by ebelle. It started as a small whitelisted community branching off of the Wings of Fire Fanon Wiki. The map, currently in its fourth iteration, is custom-made to recreate Pyrrhia and Pantala from <i>Wings of Fire</i>. The server’s story is set thousands of years following the canon events of the book series and boasts a unique cast of characters and an extensive new world full of lore to explore!
				</p>
				<p>The world has grown from under 600 blocks across to nearly 10,000.<br/>
				The staff team has grown from one person to over twenty.<br/>
				The community has grown from about thirty-five members to well over a thousand.</p>
				<h2>Check out what we’ve created!</h2>
				<SideImage imageSrc={WorldImage} imageAlt="One of the massive hives of Pantala at sunset.">
					<h3>The World of Wings of Fire</h3>
					<p>Wings of Fire: The New World is currently the <strong>largest</strong> and <strong>most complete</strong> 3D recreation of Pyrrhia and Pantala from <i>Wings of Fire</i>, and it’s entirely open for your creation!</p>
				</SideImage>
				<SideImage imageSrc={EoFImage} imageAlt="A player with flame particles emitted in a line from their face, intended to mimic flame breath." right>
					<h3>Elytras of Fire</h3>
					<p>Elytras of Fire introduces three series-inspired and all-new abilities for each tribe. Get unique powers and abilities depending on which tribe you choose to play!</p>
				</SideImage>
				<SideImage imageSrc={NPCImage} imageAlt='A non-player RainWing character named Cocoa says "Hi! You must be new around here. Welcome to Jade Mountain!"'>
					<h3>Interactive Characters</h3>
					<p>Wings of Fire: The New World features a variety of interactive non-player characters, both as part of special events as well as around the world of Pretarsi (the planet on which Pyrrhia and Pantala reside). Some have quests you can complete or items you can purchase, and all of them have unique dialogue and personalities.</p>
				</SideImage>
				<Center>
					<Button href="/gallery" secondary>
						See more images in the gallery
					</Button>
				</Center>
				<h3>We also have all this neat stuff!</h3>
				<SplitList>
					<li>Absolutely no pay walled content</li>
					<li>Advanced personal build protection</li>
					<li>Toggle pllayer combat on and off at will</li>
					<li>25 custom berries</li>
					<li>50 custom <i>Wings of Fire</i> paintings</li>
					<li>100+ custom elytra variants</li>
					<li>An economy system</li>
					<li>A shop system</li>
					<li>Discord and in-game PluralKit</li>
					<li>Sit, lay, crawl, and spin</li>
					<li>In-game roleplay and character system</li>
					<li>Discord chat bridge</li>
					<li>Dragon flight system</li>
					<li>The Block Pit resource farm</li>
					<li>The Instasmelter instant furnace</li>
					<li>And even more!</li>
				</SplitList>
				<hr />
				<Tagline>We’ve come a long way from a small server, having grown into the flourishing, ever-growing community we are today. Our staff team has continued to cultivate the server, allowing future generations of young readers to partake in a fun, safe server that they can enjoy. All staff on the server are volunteers and are very passionate about keeping both the Discord and Minecraft communities safe.</Tagline>
				<Center>
					<Group>
						<Button secondary href="/meet-the-staff">Meet the Staff Team</Button>
						<Button secondary href="https://wiki.woftnw.org/wiki/History">Learn the History</Button>
					</Group>
				</Center>
				<hr />
				<Picture src={PyrrhiaMap} alt="A map of Pyrrhia" formats={['avif', 'webp']} />
				<Picture src={PantalaMap} alt="A map of Pantala" formats={['avif', 'webp']} />
				<Center>
					<Group>
						<Button secondary href="https://map.woftnw.org/?world=minecraft_overworld&zoom=0&x=4816&z=4176">Pyrrhia Live Map</Button>
						<Button secondary href="https://map.woftnw.org/?world=woftnw_pantala&zoom=1&x=3084&z=2736">Pantala Live Map</Button>
					</Group>
				</Center>
				<Center>
					<Button href="https://woftnw.org/download-world-of-pretarsi/">Download World</Button>
				</Center>
				<h2>Want to see more? Check out our YouTube channel</h2>
				<YouTubeVideo id="OHgi3QG5C0w" title="Welcome to Wings of Fire: The New World [OFFICIAL TRAILER]" />
				<div class="split-video">
					<YouTubeVideo id="m3oFmJAB9oY" title="Project Birdhouse: Pantala Official Reveal Trailer" />
					<YouTubeVideo id="iYTKLDFH6u0" title="Frostburn War - Battle 1 Highlight Reel" />
				</div>
				<h2>Join the Community</h2>
				<p>We have a wonderful, inviting, and vibrant community that has steadily been growing. We use Discord as our primary communication platform for announcements, events, and chatting!</p>
				<p>You’ll need to read and accept Discord’s <a href="https://discord.com/terms/">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
				<Center>
					<Button href="https://discord.woftnw.org">Join the Discord</Button>
				</Center>
				<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
				<details>
					<summary>What version is the server on? What is the server's address?</summary>
					The server is running on Minecraft: Java Edition 1.21.4. Connect to it using either <em>woftnw.org</em> or <em>play.woftnw.org</em>!
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Why can't I join?</summary>
					You need to whitelist your account first! Join the Discord or send us an email. You may add usernames of friends, alt accounts, or anyone else. The server runs on Java Edition, which means you need the Windows/MacOS/Linux version of the game. Mobile, console, and other versions do not work. If the server is down or Dreamvisitor isn’t working, let the staff know and be patient; we will get to you!
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Can I join the server on bedrock?</summary>
					No, sadly. Our server software does not work with Xbox accounts, which are required for Bedrock support.
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>How can I tell if the server is online?</summary>
					You can check the status of the server at https://status.woftnw.org/. If the server has crashed, it can take up to a few days for us to fix. If we take it down, then we’re probably working on it; we will be sure to keep you guys updated!
				</details>
				<p>For more frequently asked questions, see the <a href="https://wiki.woftnw.org/wiki/WOFTNW:Frequently_Asked_Questions">wiki page</a>. If you have a question not listed, join the Discord guild or email us at contact@woftnw.org.</p>
				<LegalDisclaimer />
			</Stack>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.split-video {
		--gap-size: 20px;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 100%;
		gap: var(--gap-size);
		grid-template-rows: auto;
	}

	@media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
		.split-video {
			grid-template-columns: calc(50% - var(--gap-size)/2) calc(50% - var(--gap-size)/2);
		}
	}
</style>
